    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d14">

                <pb facs="0016" n="10" sameAs="frus:frus1942v03/pg10"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">859A.20/185: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister to the Norwegian Government in Exile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Biddle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-22T21:00:00+02:00">May 22, 1942—9
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 22—7:17 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Norwegian Series No. 9. Norwegian Government accepts in principle proposal
                    contained in your 9, May 20, 9 p.m.</p>
                <p>It desires that details of arrangement be embodied in a formal millitary
                    agreement which it hopes may be concluded at an early date.</p>
                <pb facs="0017" n="11" xml:id="pg11"/>
                <p>Norwegian Government also desires that negotiations regarding these details be
                    carried out in agreement with the British military thorities. This is necessary
                    in order to avoid any conflict with military agreements with the British which
                    regulate strength of Norwegian forces in different areas.</p>
                <closer>[<signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Biddle</hi>
                    </signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
